        "content": "#include <algorithm>\n#include <cassert>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <limits>\n#include <vector>\n\nint main() {\n    int n, s;\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; ++j) {\n            scanf(\"%d\", &matrix[i][j]);\n        }\n    }\n\n    assert(s < n);\n    assert(n < 8000);\n    assert(s > 0);\n    assert(n > 0);\n\n    long long mxSum;\n    if (s <= 2) {\n        long long sum = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < s; ++i) {\n            for (int j = 0; j < s; ++j) {\n                sum += matrix[i][j];\n            }\n        }\n        mxSum = sum;\n\n        int dir = 1;\n        int i = 0;\n        int j = 0;\n        while (i + s <= n) {\n            if ((j + s == n && dir == 1) || (j == 0 && dir == -1)) {\n                int exitingRow = i;\n                int enteringRow = exitingRow + s;\n                if (enteringRow >= n) break;\n\n                #pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum)\n                for (int k = 0; k < s; ++k) {\n                    sum += static_cast<long long>(matrix[enteringRow][k + j]) -\n                           matrix[exitingRow][k + j];\n                }\n\n                ++i;\n                dir *= -1;\n            } else {\n                int exitingCol, enteringCol;\n                if (dir == 1) {\n                    exitingCol = j;\n                    enteringCol = exitingCol + s;\n                } else {\n                    enteringCol = j - 1;\n                    exitingCol = enteringCol + s;\n                }\n\n                for (int k = 0; k < s; ++k) {\n                    sum += static_cast<long long>(matrix[k + i][enteringCol]) -\n                           matrix[k + i][exitingCol];\n                }\n                j += dir;\n            }\n            mxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\n        }\n    } else {\n        std::vector<long long> columnBand(n, 0);\n        for (int r = 0; r < s; ++r) {\n            #pragma omp simd\n            for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                columnBand[c] += matrix[r][c];\n            }\n        }\n\n        mxSum = std::numeric_limits<long long>::lowest();\n        for (int top = 0; top + s <= n; ++top) {\n            long long sum = 0;\n            #pragma omp simd reduction(+:sum)\n            for (int c = 0; c < s; ++c) {\n                sum += columnBand[c];\n            }\n            mxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\n\n            for (int left = 0; left + s < n; ++left) {\n                sum += columnBand[left + s] - columnBand[left];\n                mxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\n            }\n\n            if (top + s < n) {\n                const std::vector<int>& exitingRow = matrix[top];\n                const std::vector<int>& enteringRow = matrix[top + s];\n                #pragma omp simd\n                for (int c = 0; c < n; ++c) {\n                    columnBand[c] += static_cast<long long>(enteringRow[c]) -\n                                     exitingRow[c];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", mxSum);\n    return 0;\n}\n",
        "path": "src/solution.cpp"
      }
    ],
    "hypothesis": "Maintaining vertical column-band sums reduces repeated S-element window updates to O(N^2) work for larger windows, while SIMD over independent columns and the initial horizontal reduction can accelerate those loops. Keeping the original traversal for S <= 2 avoids extra band-maintenance work when windows are tiny.",
    "notes": "All accumulators use 64-bit signed integers to avoid intermediate overflow; the dependent horizontal rolling scan remains scalar. No commands or tests were run.",
